h-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787855390774107001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"b0a144b9-d370-49da-a2fe-b9726b50c705","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"e668-b496-e264-4283"},{"link_uuid":"0298706f-a057-4a99-a8aa-1475007c9f0c","relation":"blocks","target_id":"e668-b496-e264-4283"}],"description":"## Summary\n\nThe three-probe sandbox enforcement suite never runs on Linux in CI. It skips, silently, and a\ngreen `Verified +1` cannot be distinguished from the tests having executed.\n\n## Mechanism\n\n- `scripts/mutation_sandbox.py:113-115` records it in the merged code's own words: GitHub's\n  ubuntu runners ship bubblewrap but DENY unprivileged user namespaces\n  (`bwrap: setting up uid map: Permission denied`), so the functional probe `_bwrap_works()`\n  correctly reports no usable mechanism.\n- With `probe()` returning `None`, the `@live` skipif at `tests/scripts/test_mutation_sandbox.py:61-64`\n  fires and all four enforcement tests skip.\n- Under `-q` a skip prints as a dot-adjacent 's' and is invisible in the CI summary.\n\n## Why this matters\n\nThe macOS Seatbelt path is verified on-host (28 passed, zero skips, real deny observed). The\nLinux path is therefore an UNVERIFIED CAPABILITY: bwrap's write-deny has never been observed\nexecuting anywhere. `chiffon-venomous-annelida` AC6 was written precisely to prevent inferring\nthe Linux result from the macOS one, and it is not met.\n\n## Contradiction worth resolving\n\nTwo commits disagree. `b63cf799ed90` installs bubblewrap in the workflow specifically so these\ntests would NOT skip on Linux. `a26a73277c8a` then documents that they still find no mechanism\nthere. One of the two is stale.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The three-probe enforcement test is OBSERVED executing (not skipping) on a Linux runner,\n      with the outside-deny probe exiting non-zero and the file absent afterward.\n- [ ] If GitHub-hosted ubuntu cannot grant the required namespaces, the chosen resolution is\n      recorded with its reasoning — e.g. a different mechanism, a container with the capability,\n      or an explicit decision that Linux enforcement is out of scope.\n- [ ] A skip of these tests is made LOUD rather than silent, so a future regression to\n      'no mechanism' cannot pass as green.\n- [ ] The b63cf799ed90 / a26a73277c8a contradiction is resolved in whichever direction is true.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["blocks","e668-b496-e264-4283"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":["mutation","sandbox","ci","test-integrity"],"ticket_id":"f4c5-4354-f6b1-491e","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Mutation-sandbox enforcement tests SKIP on ubuntu-latest, so the Linux write-deny is unproven","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["0d325703-a0f1-4809-9cc8-21d5c719da6e","b0a144b9-d370-49da-a2fe-b9726b50c705","0298706f-a057-4a99-a8aa-1475007c9f0c"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787865427697289429,"uuid":"4f85a731-a179-4c7d-b471-a3e2381dce9c"}